# Gradient pre-equilibration FD-oracle fixture (issue #457, layer J of #385).
# Birth-death with a SWITCHABLE production (mirrors recovery_models/m09_preequilibration):
#   0 -> A at rate k_prod*Production_isOn,  A -> 0 at rate k_deg.
# Equilibrating with Production_isOn=1 settles A to A_ss = k_prod/k_deg; switching production
# OFF (Production_isOn=0) then makes A decay as A(t) = (k_prod/k_deg)*exp(-k_deg*t). The
# measurement's t=0 value is ENTIRELY the equilibration steady state, so the gradient of the
# measured trajectory w.r.t. k_prod flows ENTIRELY through the steady-state sensitivity seed
# (k_prod is absent from the measurement-phase RHS) -- the sharpest possible test of the
# pre-equilibration sensitivity continuity (ADR-0052 / bngsim GH #210).
begin model

begin parameters
  k_prod           3.0   # production rate
  k_deg            2.0   # degradation rate
  Production_isOn  1      # 0/1 flag: equilibrate ON, measure OFF (set inline via setParameter)
end parameters

begin molecule types
  A()
end molecule types

begin seed species
  A()  0
end seed species

begin observables
  Molecules  A_tot  A()
end observables

begin functions
  prod_rate()  k_prod * Production_isOn
end functions

begin reaction rules
  birth: 0 -> A()    prod_rate()
  death: A() -> 0    k_deg
end reaction rules

end model

begin actions
  generate_network({overwrite=>1})
end actions
